## FACT-CHECKING RULES

For every item:

1. Identify the official vendor.
2. Identify the affected product.
3. Record the exact date.
4. Include incident times and time zones when available.
5. Identify whether the incident is active, monitoring or resolved.
6. Confirm which product components were affected.
7. Link to the official source.
8. Separate confirmed facts from operational interpretation.
9. Do not assume every property was affected.
10. Do not assume a released feature is enabled.
11. Do not assume every hotel is using the newest version.
12. Do not assume an integration uses a particular API or queue.

Use labels such as:

- Confirmed by Oracle
- Confirmed by FLASH
- Operational inference
- Property confirmation required
- Vendor confirmation required
- No direct property impact confirmed

